      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling of everything being irrevocably shattered is a heavy burden to carry, and it makes perfect sense that \"reconnecting\" feels like an impossible task. When the familiar self feels gone, the void can feel absolute, like the end of a story. Instead of trying to rebuild the vase, perhaps the focus could shift to acknowledging the quiet reality of this new, fragile state. It's okay to grieve the person you were, even when that person is still fundamentally within you.",
      "source": "target",
