      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you are grappling with a deep exhaustion, where the effort required to keep going feels completely unjustified. When purpose drains away, the weight of existence can become unbearable, making the idea of letting go seem like the only logical relief. If the current state feels like nothingness, sometimes the smallest, most immediate act of self-compassion can be a starting point. Please consider reaching out to a crisis line right now; they are equipped to listen without judgment when things feel this final.",
